Drive Bracket Plate Thickness Test Procedure (rev B)
=====================================================
Document: TST-000017
Verification method: analysis
Specimen: P-000058 drive bracket (single Part instance)
Approved by: test engineer (sign-off) + methodology reviewer (sign-off)

Procedure:
  1. Visually inspect specimen for surface defects per the inspection checklist.
  2. Place specimen in Instron 5944 calibrated fixture (calibration certificate
     CAL-2026-Q1-031).
  3. Measure plate thickness at three points along the central beam axis using
     a Mitutoyo digital micrometer (accuracy +/- 0.005 mm); record each
     per-point reading.
  4. Compute mean thickness; report as `measured_thickness_mm` field on the
     resulting EvidenceArtifact sidecar.
  5. Verify that `measured_thickness_mm` >= 5.0 mm per the `ac_min_thickness`
     acceptance criterion of REQ-000058.

Environmental conditions: ambient lab 20-24 degC, 30-50% relative humidity.
Expected output: one EvidenceArtifact (evidence_kind: measurement) carrying
                 `reported_thickness_mm` and one TestExecution recording the
                 run (execution_status: completed when no anomalies).
